      "content": "That makes sense. The risk of brown rot and beetle damage is definitely top of mind for us. \n\nHowever, I'm also looking for less \"biological\" or standard environmental explanations. Are there any other peculiar or highly irregular failure modes you've encountered—things that seem to defy standard material science or appear almost like \"sabotage\" or inexplicable structural weakness that doesn't immediately trace back to rot or pests? We're trying to identify any outliers that could lead to a sudden loss of integrity.",
